// The traversal of WoSX's GPU kernel on its default tree: FCPW's binary BVH
// in FCPW's bytes (layouts/fcpwb.bonsai), the walk a loop, the closest-point
// traversal on a stack of FCPW's depth with the two children tested at their
// parent and the nearer entered first, the leaf's Voronoi arms skipped where
// the point is not in them. The key is the child's squared distance to its
// box, FCPW's d2Min, and a tie keeps the left child first: bvh.slang's
// `if (distToChildNodes[2] < distToChildNodes[0]) swap` and nothing else --
// where FCPW's CPU traversal, which fcpwb.bonsai follows, orders two
// children that both contain the point by their far corners instead. The
// GPU schedules (fcpwb-gpu*.bonsai) import this file for the traversal and
// add how the walks are run.
import apps/wosx/schedules/layouts/fcpwb;

schedule {
    walk.loopify();
    closest_within.sort(triangles.Interior,
                        |i : u32, s : Sphere, lo : vector[vec3f, 2], hi : vector[vec3f, 2]|
                        distmin(s, AABB{lo[i], hi[i]}))
                  .loopify(64);
    closest_within.skip(closest_point_fcpw);
}
